    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0441" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg359"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 21, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose for your information a copy of a
                    despatch of the 12th ultimo, No. 208, from Charles A. Leas, esq., the United
                    States commercial agent at <pb facs="0442" n="360" xml:id="pg360"/> Belize, in
                    regard to a recent proclamation of Prince Maximilian affecting the British
                    settlement in Honduras, and relating also to other features of political affairs
                    in that quarter and the West Indies.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chargé d’ Affaires of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
